# A dynamic at an element's plain (identity) field lifts the construction to a
# `$Element o`, which a `let` may hold; only a statement that would build it refuses, at the
# field, with the `rebuild` fix (Type System ch. 2-05, "A dynamic in an identity field lifts
# the construction to `$Element o`, and the statement refuses it"; neg identity-dynamic).
# Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*

@pictures: @unit
@pictures:
    !go <- Ui.Button($label=$"Next")
    $src <- "a.png" then "b.png" on !go
    let $image = Ui.Image(src=$src)
    rebuild $src:
        Ui.Image(src=_)
